<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna varargsave: a System V variadic function's register save area.

    Source (gcc -O2):

        void log_msg(const char *fmt, ...) {
          va_list ap; va_start(ap, fmt); vfprintf(stderr, fmt, ap); va_end(ap);
        }

        401174  sub  rsp,0xd8
        40117b  mov  [rsp+0x28],rsi ... mov [rsp+0x48],r9   ; save+8*i
        401194  test al,al
        401196  je   4011cf
        401198  movaps [rsp+0x50],xmm0 ... [rsp+0xc0],xmm7  ; save+48+16*j
        4011cf  ...va_start, then __vfprintf_chk(stderr,1,fmt,&ap)

    Every save-area store reads an argument register, so input recovery gave
    log_msg fourteen parameters (all six integer and eight vector argument
    registers), the body opened with their copies, and `if (al)` tested an
    undefined byte.

    Stage: P4 prototype (ActionStart, before heritage), option varargsave
    off|on.  Pass 1 (off) pins the bug, pass 2 (on, the default) the fix.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401170">

</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x401040">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401170" name="log_msg"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x401040" name="__vfprintf_chk"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x404020" name="stderr"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option varargsave off</com>
  <com>lo fu log_msg</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option varargsave on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="VARARGSAVE #1: off, every argument register is a parameter" min="1" max="1">log_msg\([^)]*a13\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARARGSAVE #2: on, one named parameter and the ellipsis" min="1" max="1">void log_msg\(\w[\w ]*\*?\w+,\.\.\.\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARARGSAVE #3: on, no test of the vector count" min="1" max="1">if \(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARARGSAVE #4: on, the va_list set-up is va_start on a local" min="1" max="1">  va_start\(&amp;?\w+\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="VARARGSAVE #5: both passes, the callee receives the va_list" min="2" max="2">__vfprintf_chk\(\w+,1,\w+,&amp;?\w+\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
